	ü What are keywords in JavaScript ?

	• Keywords are reserved words in JS that has special meaning attached to it for the language 

	• These we cannot use for naming a variable 

	• Example of keywords like : if, else, else if , for, while, let, var, const etc.

	ü What are identifiers and Literals ?

	· Identifiers are the name given to any variable, class, method etc.

	• Literals are the values given to that variable that we defined 

	Ex:
	   let my_name = 'Amrit Manash'
	
   here my_name is identifier and Amrit Manash is literal 
